## Architecture Design:
A single, shared Transformer encoder learns general representations.
Two separate dense Linear projection layers sit on top of the shared [CLS] token output:
Head A: Classifies Hate Speech.
Head B: Classifies Irony.
## Testing Methodology
Shared Gradient Updates: In every step (or every few steps), gradients flow backwards from both heads into the shared Transformer backbone.
Loss Weighting (α): The combined loss is formulated as:

